Package: faceid-nim
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libpam-runtime, python3 (>= 3.10),
 policykit-1 | polkitd, dbus, adduser
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Suggests: linux-enable-ir-emitter
Description: Face unlock for Ubuntu with a lock-screen animation
 Face unlock via PAM, backed by a privileged daemon and an unprivileged
 vision worker, with a GNOME Shell pill showing scan state.
 .
 This is a convenience feature, not Face ID. On an ordinary RGB webcam
 it can be defeated by a good video replay; an infrared camera is
 substantially stronger. Your password always continues to work.
 .
 Face unlock is installed disabled and stays off until you enable it in
 the Face Unlock app.
